"""Authored session sequence. Software implementation precedes mathematical detail."""
MODULES=[
('Module 1 · Modern AI Stack & Foundational APIs','Weeks 1–2',1,6,
 'A real-time voice assistant with bidirectional PCM audio, concurrent input/output and explicit interruption/reconnect behavior.',
 '''Start with an application boundary: an authenticated user asks a question, an adapter sends a bounded request, a stream returns draft events and the application validates/persists the result. Choose capabilities before vendor branding: text, audio input/output, tool calling, context size, residency, quotas and measured latency all affect the interface. An SDK hides transport details but cannot choose your retry policy, trust boundary or quality standard.

Stateless requests carry their selected history each time. Stateful sessions retain provider-side state but still need tenant ownership, expiry, consent and a recovery path. Input token counts are a preflight tool; output/reasoning/tool/cached usage belongs in the completed run record when the provider supplies it. A character or word estimate can help reject obviously oversized work, but it is not measured billing.

Concurrency is a capacity decision. Bounded queues and semaphores prevent a burst of users from becoming unlimited simultaneous provider calls. Cancellation must stop children and release resources when a browser leaves. Set both per-operation timeout and overall deadline; backoff and queue wait consume that deadline. Do not replay an external write merely because a network response was lost.

In voice, separate capture rate, wire encoding, provider input format and playback format. Raw PCM16 is not WebM/Opus. Measure microphone capture → gateway enqueue → provider first audio → audible playback, with a defined start event such as end of speech. A low first-token time can coexist with an unusable playback backlog. Interruptions must clear scheduled sound as well as server generation. Reconnect state is a lifecycle problem rather than permission to replay arbitrary frames.

The supplied gateway includes a visible offline echo mode for protocol testing and an opt-in Gemini adapter. Echo establishes transport/cancellation behavior only; live task correctness, speech intelligibility, provider billing and network latency remain unmeasured until you run an authorized evaluation. Keep server credentials out of browser bundles, require session authorization, restrict origins and impose per-session byte/time/concurrency limits. Record installed SDK and model versions; availability changes, so the model is an explicit configuration value.'''),
('Module 2 · Data Grounding & Advanced RAG','Weeks 3–5',7,15,
 'A mixed-media knowledge base with owner-scoped uploads, provenance, hybrid/re-ranked retrieval and source-grounded streaming answers.',
 '''Treat retrieval as a data product with explicit lifecycle states: received, parsed, chunked, embedded, indexed, evaluated and active. Upload success is not search readiness. A failed replacement revision must not remove the last working active index. Preserve original digest, owner, source revision and page/paragraph/timestamp locators before normalization.

PDF extraction can fail on scans; DOCX can contain tables or large decompressed archives; websites can redirect to unintended hosts; transcripts need time anchors and permissioned provenance. The complete parser handles text PDFs, DOCX paragraphs/tables, approved-origin HTML and supplied VTT transcripts. It deliberately rejects an unreadable scan rather than claiming OCR. Run CPU/untrusted parsers in bounded workers with page/byte/time limits instead of blocking an async request loop.

Chunking is an engineering trade-off. Fixed token windows are reproducible; heading/semantic boundaries can preserve meaning but add cost or variability. Compare retrieval and answer support on the same cases. Keep exceptions and applicability conditions attached, budget metadata and output reserve, and record offsets so a reviewer can inspect the original evidence.

Embedding model/version/dimension and normalization form an index contract. A model migration requires a parallel index and a measured promotion decision, not mixing vectors. Start with exact tenant-filtered search. Approximate indexes can trade recall for latency and may return too few authorized results after filtering. Use actual execution plans and relevance labels when tuning HNSW rather than memorizing a parameter.

Hybrid retrieval combines complementary candidate lists. Reciprocal-rank fusion avoids assuming lexical and vector scores share a scale. A reranker can reorder a bounded candidate set but cannot recover absent evidence. Its extra latency and spend must fit the remaining deadline and demonstrate useful quality gain. Citation membership proves identity; factual support and correct policy applicability require separate review. Stream draft text with explicit complete/error events, and never cache a partial answer as final. A source-grounded chat capstone earns its claim through owner isolation, provenance, no-answer behavior, revision activation, evaluation and recovery—not by resembling a chat interface.'''),
('Module 3 · Agentic Workflows & Multi-Agent Systems','Weeks 6–8',16,24,
 'A scoped workspace agent that monitors a test channel, drafts from an authorized knowledge base and prepares/reviews calendar actions.',
 '''An agent chooses proposed steps from observations; application code controls what those steps can do. Begin with a fixed retrieval/draft pipeline and add a bounded loop only for an observed need. Tool binding supplies names and schemas, while the dispatcher supplies authenticated identity, allowed scope, argument validation and stable error categories. Gmail/Slack/calendar credentials, channel membership and calendar ownership remain outside model-generated arguments.

Represent workflow state explicitly: queued, retrieving, drafting, awaiting review, approved, claimed, committed, uncertain or failed. Durable checkpoints belong outside process memory. LangGraph exposes graph state, checkpoints and interrupts; LangChain helps compose models/tools; CrewAI offers role/task coordination. Compare each against the simpler workflow using correctness, recovery, latency, cost and maintenance. A second model persona does not create durability or authority.

Human approval binds the exact payload, actor, destination, revision and expiry. Resuming a graph may rerun a node; perform irreversible work only behind an authorized idempotent boundary. A database transaction can atomically update local records but cannot unsend an email. After a remote timeout, reconcile the existing operation key and outcome before any retry. Remote APIs differ in duplicate-prevention guarantees.

Memory should be selected by owner, source revision and relevance. Summaries can omit exceptions or stale facts; keep recoverable originals and evaluate compression on factual cases. Delegation helps independent work only when parallel latency or quality gains justify duplicate context and calls. Preserve branch provenance and define conflict arbitration rather than concatenating confident narratives.

MCP introduces a host/client/server contract for tools, resources and prompts. Discovery metadata is untrusted capability description, not permission. Negotiate capabilities, validate tool results and enforce actual actor scope. Webhook monitoring similarly needs signature/replay validation, durable inbox IDs, rapid acknowledgement and a bounded worker queue. The capstone can monitor and propose autonomously within its configured read scope; sending messages and creating invitations require the reviewed effect contract. Use local fake destinations first, and only opt into your own authorized test accounts. This course does not send messages or schedule events on your behalf.'''),
('Module 4 · LLMOps, Evaluation & Observability','Weeks 9–10',25,30,
 'A release evaluation service with at least 120 concrete labeled edge cases, CI gates, traces and latency/cost/quality reports.',
 '''Define the claim before the metric. Faithfulness concerns whether claims are supported by retrieved context; relevance concerns the user question; retrieval recall concerns whether needed evidence was found. None alone certifies an application. Include exact schema/permission/state checks, category-level relevance labels and reviewed semantic rubrics rather than one score labeled AI accuracy.

Deterministic evaluation means repeatable automated contracts and measurement rules over versioned inputs. A model judge remains a model: record its version, prompt, configuration, failures and disagreement with human review. Ragas/TruLens can automate semantic scoring, but they do not turn uncertain labels into ground truth. Use an explicit calibration set, preserve difficult examples and audit the strongest failure.

The evaluation suite contains 100+ actual inputs, not only generated IDs. Each needs expected behavior, source/actor state, criticality and evidence. Split by case families to reduce paraphrase leakage; once a holdout failure influences a fix, relabel it as development evidence and obtain fresh cases for new claims. Retain unavailable runs and malformed outputs in denominators.

A release manifest binds code, SDK/model, prompt, dataset, parser, context policy, index and judge revisions. Fast deterministic checks run on every change; budgeted live evaluations run in a separate authorized CI job. Promotion requires critical failures to be resolved even when the aggregate score improves. Store case-level results, duration, usage type and actual spend inputs with the report.

Observability should expose the failing stage without exporting private prompts. Distinguish queue wait, retrieval, provider first output, retries, validation and review. Parallel spans cannot be summed as wall time. Trace exporters such as LangSmith/Phoenix need payload minimization, consent/access and retention policies too. The capstone must block a deliberately regressed candidate, reproduce its cause, implement a correction and retain before/after evidence. Context size, cache policy and model routing are then optimized against accepted-output quality, not a selected fast demo.'''),
('Module 5 · Scaling, Hosting & Edge Deployment','Weeks 11–12',31,36,
 'A deployed hybrid-model SaaS candidate with tenant isolation, measured load envelope, quotas, recovery and an explicit release decision.',
 '''A production candidate joins interface, API, persistence, provider/local inference, queues, secrets, traces and operational ownership. The local Docker experiment teaches network and storage boundaries; graduating requires applying those boundaries to the full authenticated app. Built frontend behavior, actual database readiness, migrations, restart/readback and an isolated restore are part of release evidence.

Choose a hosting path deliberately. Cloud Run maps request concurrency and instance limits to containerized work; WebSockets still have request timeouts and reconnects may reach a different instance. ECS adds task/service/load-balancer choices, health checks and draining. On either, state and quotas must survive a process and multiple replicas. Keep database connection limits and downstream provider quotas in the capacity plan.

Configured concurrency is not measured hardware capacity. Test offered load, admitted/completed work, failures, queue depth and p95 with quality and spend visible. Increasing a concurrency flag may only create longer waits or GPU memory failures. Maximum instance and budget caps bound potential spend but can force rejection under load. Report the actual tested envelope; a target of thousands of users remains a target until observed under defined conditions.

Self-hosted open models move operations and cost to local/GPU infrastructure. Account for model artifacts/licensing, quantization, resident weights, runtime buffers, KV cache, context length, batching, cold load and monitoring. Ollama provides a local serving route; vLLM serves supported models with batching controls. Compare exact deployed artifacts using the same quality set; neither low marginal API cost nor an OpenAI-compatible shape establishes equivalent behavior.

Rate limits, token reservations, work concurrency and monetary budgets are separate controls. Use shared atomic enforcement across replicas; evaluate limiter-store failure modes and reconciliation of reserved versus observed usage. Hybrid routing must preserve owner/data-residency boundaries and response contracts. A premium fallback is not permission to disclose data approved only for local processing. The final handover includes quality/latency/cost results, 120-case evaluation, context/cache manifest, incident/restore drill, ownership and unresolved blockers. Production readiness is a decision supported by observed evidence, not a certificate issued because a demo deploys.'''),
]
